(6) Tj T*
(Introduction: From Prototype) Tj T*
(to Production) Tj T*
(You can spin up an AI agent prototype in minutes, maybe even seconds. But turning that) Tj T*
(clever demo into a trusted, production-grade system that your business can depend on?) Tj T*
(That's where the real work begins. Welcome to the "last mile" production gap, where we) Tj T*
(consistently observe in practice with customers that roughly 80% of the effort is spent not) Tj T*
(on the agent's core intelligence, but on the infrastructure, security, and validation needed to) Tj T*
(make it reliable and safe.) Tj T*
(Skipping these final steps could cause several problems. For example:) Tj T*
(* A customer service agent is tricked into giving products away for free because you) Tj T*
(forgot to set up the right guardrails.) Tj T*
(* A user discovers they can access a confidential internal database through your agent) Tj T*
(because authentication was improperly configured.) Tj T*
(* An agent generates a large consumption bill over the weekend, but no one knows why) Tj T*
(because you didn't set up any monitoring.) Tj T*
(* A critical agent that worked perfectly yesterday suddenly stops, but your team is) Tj T*
(scrambling because there was no continuous evaluation in place.) Tj T*
(These aren't just technical problems; they are major business failures. And while principles) Tj T*
(from DevOps and MLOps provide a critical foundation, they aren't enough on their own.) Tj T*
(Deploying agentic systems introduces a new class of challenges that require an evolution) Tj T*
(in our operational discipline. Unlike traditional ML models, agents are autonomously) Tj T*
(interactive, stateful, and follow dynamic execution paths.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
