(9) Tj T*
(Figure 1: A diagram showing that "Ops" is the intersection of people, processes, and technology) Tj T*
(In a traditional MLOps landscape, this involves several key teams:) Tj T*
(* Cloud Platform Team: Comprising cloud architects, administrators, and security) Tj T*
(specialists, this team manages the foundational cloud infrastructure, security, and access) Tj T*
(control. The team grants engineers and service accounts least-privilege roles, ensuring) Tj T*
(access only to necessary resources.) Tj T*
(* Data Engineering Team: Data engineers and data owners build and maintain the data) Tj T*
(pipelines, handling ingestion, preparation, and quality standards.) Tj T*
(* Data Science and MLOps Team: This includes data scientists who experiment with) Tj T*
(and train models, and ML engineers who automate the end-to-end ML pipeline \(e.g.,) Tj T*
(preprocessing, training, post-processing\) at scale using CI/CD. MLOps Engineers support) Tj T*
(this by building and maintaining the standardized pipeline infrastructure.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
