(10) Tj T*
(* Machine Learning Governance: This centralized function, including product owners) Tj T*
(and auditors, oversees the ML lifecycle, acting as a repository for artifacts and metrics to) Tj T*
(ensure compliance, transparency, and accountability .) Tj T*
(Generative AI introduces a new layer of complexity and specialized roles to this landscape:) Tj T*
(* Prompt Engineers: While this role title is still evolving in the industry, these individuals) Tj T*
(blend technical skill in crafting prompts with deep domain expertise. They define the) Tj T*
(right questions and expected answers from a model, though in practice this work may) Tj T*
(be done by AI Engineers, domain experts, or dedicated specialists depending on the) Tj T*
(organization's maturity.) Tj T*
(* AI Engineers: They are responsible for scaling GenAI solutions to production, building) Tj T*
(robust backend systems that incorporate evaluation at scale, guardrails, and RAG/tool) Tj T*
(integration .) Tj T*
(* DevOps/App Developers: These developers build the front-end components and user-) Tj T*
(friendly interfaces that integrate with the GenAI backend.) Tj T*
(The scale and structure of an organization will influence these roles; in smaller companies,) Tj T*
(individuals may wear multiple hats, while mature organizations will have more specialized) Tj T*
(teams. Effectively coordinating all these diverse roles is essential for establishing a robust) Tj T*
(operational foundation and successfully productionizing both traditional ML and generative) Tj T*
(AI initiatives.) Tj T*
ET
