(12) Tj T*
(Evaluation as a Quality Gate) Tj T*
(Why do we need a special quality gate for agents? Traditional software tests are insufficient) Tj T*
(for systems that reason and adapt. Furthermore, evaluating an agent is distinct from) Tj T*
(evaluating an LLM; it requires assessing not just the final answer, but the entire trajectory) Tj T*
(of reasoning and actions taken to complete a task. An agent can pass 100 unit tests for its) Tj T*
(tools but still fail spectacularly by choosing the wrong tool or hallucinating a response. We) Tj T*
(need to evaluate its behavioral quality, not just its functional correctness. This gate can be) Tj T*
(implemented in two primary ways:) Tj T*
(1. The Manual "Pre-PR" Evaluation: For teams seeking flexibility or just beginning their) Tj T*
(evaluation journey, the quality gate is enforced through a team process. Before submitting) Tj T*
(a pull request \(PR\), the AI Engineer or Prompt Engineer \(or whoever is responsible) Tj T*
(for agent behavior in your organization\) runs the evaluation suite locally. The resulting) Tj T*
(performance report--comparing the new agent against the production baseline--is then) Tj T*
(linked in the PR description. This makes the evaluation results a mandatory artifact for) Tj T*
(human review. The reviewer--typically another AI Engineer or the Machine Learning) Tj T*
(Governor--is now responsible for assessing not just the code, but also the agent's) Tj T*
(behavioral changes against guardrail violations and prompt injection vulnerabilities.) Tj T*
(2. The Automated In-Pipeline Gate: For mature teams, the evaluation harness--built and) Tj T*
(maintained by the Data Science and MLOps Team--is integrated directly into the CI/) Tj T*
(CD pipeline. A failing evaluation automatically blocks the deployment, providing rigid,) Tj T*
(programmatic enforcement of quality standards that the Machine Learning Governance) Tj T*
(team has defined. This approach trades the flexibility of manual review for the consistency) Tj T*
(of automation. The CI/CD pipeline can be configured to automatically trigger an evaluation) Tj T*
(job that compares the new agent's responses against a golden dataset. The deployment is) Tj T*
(programmatically blocked if key metrics, such as "tool call success rate" or "helpfulness,") Tj T*
(fall below a predefined threshold.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
