(Page 17 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(17) Tj T*
(Building Security from the Start) Tj T*
(Safe deployment strategies protect you from bugs and outages, but agents face a unique) Tj T*
(challenge: they can reason and act autonomously. A perfectly deployed agent can still cause) Tj T*
(harm if it hasn't been built with proper security and responsibility measures. This requires a) Tj T*
(comprehensive governance strategy embedded from day one, not added as an afterthought.) Tj T*
(Unlike traditional software that follows predetermined paths, agents make decisions. They) Tj T*
(interpret ambiguous requests, access multiple tools, and maintain memory across sessions.) Tj T*
(This autonomy creates distinct risks:) Tj T*
(* Prompt Injection & Rogue Actions: Malicious users can trick agents into performing) Tj T*
(unintended actions or bypassing restrictions.) Tj T*
(* Data Leakage: Agents might inadvertently expose sensitive information through their) Tj T*
(responses or tool usage.) Tj T*
(* Memory Poisoning: False information stored in an agent's memory can corrupt all) Tj T*
(future interactions.) Tj T*
(Fortunately, frameworks like Google's Secure AI Agents approach12 and the Google Secure) Tj T*
(AI Framework \(SAIF\)13 address these challenges through three layers of defense:) Tj T*
(1. Policy Definition and System Instructions \(The Agent's Constitution\): The process) Tj T*
(begins by defining policies for desired and undesired agent behavior. These are) Tj T*
(engineered into System Instructions \(SIs\) that act as the agent's core constitution.) Tj T*
(2. Guardrails, Safeguards, and Filtering \(The Enforcement Layer\): This layer acts as the) Tj T*
(hard-stop enforcement mechanism.) Tj T*
(* Input Filtering: Use classifiers and services like the Perspective API to analyze prompts) Tj T*
(and block malicious inputs before they reach the agent.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
