(Page 19 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(19) Tj T*
(Operations in-Production) Tj T*
(Your agent is live. Now the focus shifts from development to a fundamentally different) Tj T*
(challenge: keeping the system reliable, cost-effective, and safe as it interacts with) Tj T*
(thousands of users. A traditional service operates on predictable logic. An agent, in) Tj T*
(contrast, is an autonomous actor. Its ability to follow unexpected reasoning paths means it) Tj T*
(can exhibit emergent behaviors and accumulate costs without direct oversight.) Tj T*
(Managing this autonomy requires a different operational model. Instead of static monitoring,) Tj T*
(effective teams adopt a continuous loop: Observe the system's behavior in real-time, Act to) Tj T*
(maintain performance and safety, and Evolve the agent based on production learnings. This) Tj T*
(integrated cycle is the core discipline for operating agents successfully in production.) Tj T*
(Observe: Your Agent's Sensory System) Tj T*
(To trust and manage an autonomous agent, you must first understand its process.) Tj T*
(Observability provides this crucial insight, acting as the sensory system for the subsequent) Tj T*
("Act" and "Evolve" phases. A robust observability practice is built on three pillars that work) Tj T*
(together to provide a complete picture of the agent's behavior:) Tj T*
(* Logs: The granular, factual diary of what happened, recording every tool call, error,) Tj T*
(and decision.) Tj T*
(* Traces: The narrative that connects individual logs, revealing the causal path of why an) Tj T*
(agent took a certain action.) Tj T*
(* Metrics: The aggregated report card, summarizing performance, cost, and operational) Tj T*
(health at scale to show how well the system is performing.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
