(Page 21 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(21) Tj T*
(* Designing for Scale: The foundation is decoupling the agent's logic from its state.) Tj T*
(* Horizontal Scaling: Design the agent as a stateless, containerized service. With) Tj T*
(external state, any instance can handle any request, enabling serverless platforms like) Tj T*
(Cloud Run10 or the managed Vertex AI Agent Engine Runtime9 to scale automatically.) Tj T*
(* Asynchronous Processing: For long-running tasks, offload work using event-) Tj T*
(driven patterns. This keeps the agent responsive while complex jobs process in the) Tj T*
(background. On Google Cloud, for example, a service can publish tasks to Pub/Sub19,) Tj T*
(which can then trigger a Cloud Run service for asynchronous processing.) Tj T*
(* Externalized State Management: Since LLMs are stateless, persisting memory) Tj T*
(externally is non-negotiable. This highlights a key architectural choice: Agent Runtime) Tj T*
(provides built-in Sessions and a Memory Bank for persistent, long-term context across) Tj T*
(multi-day workflows, while Cloud Run offers the flexibility to integrate directly with) Tj T*
(databases like AlloyDB20 or Cloud SQL21.) Tj T*
(* Balancing Competing Goals: Scaling always involves balancing three competing goals:) Tj T*
(speed, reliability, and cost.) Tj T*
(* Speed \(Latency\): Keep your agent fast by designing it to work in parallel, aggressively) Tj T*
(caching results, and using smaller, efficient models for routine tasks.) Tj T*
(* Reliability \(Handling Glitches\): Agents must handle temporary failures. When a call) Tj T*
(fails, automatically retry, ideally with exponential backoff to give the service time to) Tj T*
(recover. This requires designing "safe-to-retry" \(idempotent\) tools to prevent bugs like) Tj T*
(duplicate charges.) Tj T*
(* Cost: Keep the agent affordable by shortening prompts, using cheaper models for) Tj T*
(easier tasks, and sending requests in groups \(batching\).) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
