(Page 23 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(23) Tj T*
(The Engine of Evolution: An Automated Path to Production) Tj T*
(An insight from production is only valuable if you can act on it quickly. Observing that 30% of) Tj T*
(your users fail at a specific task is useless if it takes your team six months to deploy a fix.) Tj T*
(This is where the automated CI/CD pipeline you built in pre-production \(Section 3\)) Tj T*
(becomes the most critical component of your operational loop. It is the engine that powers) Tj T*
(rapid evolution. A fast, reliable path to production allows you to close the loop between) Tj T*
(observation and improvement in hours or days, not weeks or months.) Tj T*
(When you identify a potential improvement--whether it's a refined prompt, a new tool, or an) Tj T*
(updated safety guardrail--the process should be:) Tj T*
(1. Commit the Change: The proposed improvement is committed to your) Tj T*
(version-controlled repository.) Tj T*
(2. Trigger Automation: The commit automatically triggers your CI/CD pipeline.) Tj T*
(3. Validate Rigorously: The pipeline runs the full suite of unit tests, security scans, and the) Tj T*
(agent quality evaluation suite against your updated datasets.) Tj T*
(4. Deploy Safely: Once validated, the change is deployed to production using a safe) Tj T*
(rollout strategy.) Tj T*
(This automated workflow transforms evolution from a slow, high-risk manual project into a) Tj T*
(fast, repeatable, and data-driven process.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
