(Page 25 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(25) Tj T*
(Evolving Security: The Production Feedback Loop) Tj T*
(While the foundational security and responsibility framework is established in pre-production) Tj T*
(\(Section 3.4\), the work is never truly finished. Security is not a static checklist; it is a dynamic,) Tj T*
(continuous process of adaptation. The production environment is the ultimate testing) Tj T*
(ground, and the insights gathered there are essential for hardening your agent against) Tj T*
(real-world threats.) Tj T*
(This is where the Observe -> Act -> Evolve loop becomes critical for security. The process) Tj T*
(is a direct extension of the evolution workflow:) Tj T*
(1. Observe: Your monitoring and logging systems detect a new threat vector. This could be) Tj T*
(a novel prompt injection technique that bypasses your current filters, or an unexpected) Tj T*
(interaction that leads to a minor data leak.) Tj T*
(2. Act: The immediate security response team contains the threat \(as discussed in) Tj T*
(Section 4.2\).) Tj T*
(3. Evolve: This is the crucial step for long-term resilience. The security insight is fed back) Tj T*
(into your development lifecycle:) Tj T*
(* Update Evaluation Datasets: The new prompt injection attack is added as a) Tj T*
(permanent test case to your evaluation suite.) Tj T*
(* Refine Guardrails: A Prompt Engineer or AI Engineer refines the agent's system) Tj T*
(prompt, input filters, or tool-use policies to block the new attack vector.) Tj T*
(* Automate and Deploy: The engineer commits the change, which triggers the full CI/) Tj T*
(CD pipeline. The updated agent is rigorously validated against the newly expanded) Tj T*
(evaluation set and deployed to production, closing the vulnerability.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
