/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 30 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(30) Tj T*
(Snippet 2: Using the ADK's to_a2a utility to wrap an existing agent and expose it for A2A communication) Tj T*
(Once an agent is exposed, any other agent can consume it by referencing its AgentCard. For) Tj T*
(example, a customer service agent can now query a remote product catalog agent without) Tj T*
(needing to know its internal workings.) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(# Example using ADK: Exposing an agent via A2A) Tj T*
(from google.adk.a2a.utils.agent_to_a2a import to_a2a) Tj T*
(# Your existing agent) Tj T*
(root_agent = Agent\() Tj T*
(name='hello_world_agent',) Tj T*
(# ... your agent code ...) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(# Make it A2A-compatible) Tj T*
(a2a_app = to_a2a\(root_agent, port=8001\)) Tj T*
(# Serve with uvicorn) Tj T*
(# uvicorn agent:a2a_app --host localhost --port 8001) Tj T*
(# Or serve with Agent Engine) Tj T*
(# from vertexai.preview.reasoning_engines import A2aAgent) Tj T*
(# from google.adk.a2a.executor.a2a_agent_executor import A2aAgentExecutor) Tj T*
(# a2a_agent = A2aAgent\() Tj T*
(#    agent_executor_builder=lambda: A2aAgentExecutor\(agent=root_agent\)) Tj T*
(# \)) Tj T*
ET
endstream
