stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
36 756 Td
13 TL
(Page 32 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(32) Tj T*
(Snippet 4: Using a remote A2A agent \(prime_agent\) as a sub-agent within a hierarchical agent structure in) Tj T*
(the ADK) Tj T*
(However, enabling this level of autonomous collaboration introduces two non-negotiable) Tj T*
(technical requirements. First is distributed tracing, where every request carries a unique) Tj T*
(trace ID, which is essential for debugging and maintaining a coherent audit trail across) Tj T*
(multiple agents. Second is robust state management. A2A interactions are inherently) Tj T*
(stateful, requiring a sophisticated persistence layer for tracking progress and ensuring) Tj T*
(transactional integrity.) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(# Example using ADK: Hierarchical agent composition) Tj T*
(# ADK Local sub-agent for dice rolling) Tj T*
(roll_agent = Agent\() Tj T*
(name="roll_agent",) Tj T*
(instruction="You are an expert at rolling dice.") Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(# ADK Remote A2A agent for prime checking) Tj T*
(prime_agent = RemoteA2aAgent\() Tj T*
(name="prime_agent",) Tj T*
(agent_card="http://localhost:8001/.well-known/agent-card.json") Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
(# ADK Root orchestrator combining both) Tj T*
(root_agent = Agent\() Tj T*
(name="root_agent",) Tj T*
(instruction="""Delegate rolling dice to roll_agent, prime checking) Tj T*
(to prime_agent.""",) Tj T*
(sub_agents=[roll_agent, prime_agent]) Tj T*
(\)) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
