(Page 33 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(33) Tj T*
(A2A is best suited for formal, cross-team integrations that require a durable service) Tj T*
(contract. For tightly coupled tasks within a single application, lightweight local sub-agents) Tj T*
(often remain a more efficient choice. As the ecosystem matures, new agents should be) Tj T*
(built with native support for both protocols, ensuring every new component is immediately) Tj T*
(discoverable, interoperable, and reusable, compounding the value of the whole system.) Tj T*
(How A2A and MCP Work Together) Tj T*
(Figure 4: A2A and MCP collaboration with a single glance) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
