(Page 35 of 41 - Prototype to  Production) Tj T*
(Prototype to Production) Tj T*
(Updated May 2026) Tj T*
(35) Tj T*
(In this workflow, A2A facilitates the higher-level, conversational, and task-oriented) Tj T*
(interactions between the customer, the shop's agents, and external suppliers. Meanwhile,) Tj T*
(MCP provides the standardized plumbing that enables the mechanic agent to reliably use its) Tj T*
(specific, structured tools to do its job.) Tj T*
(Registry Architectures: When and How to Build Them) Tj T*
(Why do some organizations build registries while others don't need them? The answer lies in) Tj T*
(scale and complexity. When you have fifty tools, manual configuration works fine. But when) Tj T*
(you reach five thousand tools distributed across different teams and environments, you face) Tj T*
(a discovery problem that demands a systematic solution.) Tj T*
(To solve these discovery and governance challenges at scale, the Gemini Enterprise Agent) Tj T*
(Platform provides a native Agent Registry. This centralized catalog allows teams to discover,) Tj T*
(track, and manage all agents, tools, and MCP servers across the organization. Paired) Tj T*
(with Agent Identity--which assigns a unique cryptographic ID to every agent--it enables) Tj T*
(robust governance and secure access control out of the box. However, if you are building) Tj T*
(outside of this integrated ecosystem, understanding the underlying registry architecture) Tj T*
(remains critical.) Tj T*
(A Tool Registry uses a protocol like MCP to catalog all assets, from functions to APIs.) Tj T*
(Instead of giving agents access to thousands of tools, you create curated lists, leading to) Tj T*
(three common patterns:) Tj T*
(* Generalist agents: Access the full catalog, trading speed and accuracy for scope.) Tj T*
(* Specialist agents: Use predefined subsets for higher performance.) Tj T*
(* Dynamic agents: Query the registry at runtime to adapt to new tools.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
