(38) Tj T*
(Conclusion: Bridging the Last Mile) Tj T*
(with AgentOps) Tj T*
(Moving an AI prototype to a production system is an organizational transformation that) Tj T*
(requires a new operational discipline: AgentOps.) Tj T*
(Most agent projects fail in the "last mile" not due to technology, but because the operational) Tj T*
(complexity of autonomous systems is underestimated. This guide maps the path to bridge) Tj T*
(that gap. It begins with establishing People and Process as the foundation for governance.) Tj T*
(Next, a Pre-Production strategy built on evaluation-gated deployment automates high-) Tj T*
(stakes releases. Once live, a continuous Observe -> Act -> Evolve loop turns every user) Tj T*
(interaction into a potential insight. Finally, Interoperability protocols scale the system by) Tj T*
(transforming isolated agents into a collaborative, intelligent ecosystem.) Tj T*
(The immediate benefits--like preventing a security breach or enabling a rapid rollback--) Tj T*
(justify the investment. But the real value is velocity. Mature AgentOps practices allow teams) Tj T*
(to deploy improvements in hours, not weeks, turning static deployments into continuously) Tj T*
(evolving products.) Tj T*
(Your Path Forward) Tj T*
(* If you're starting out, focus on the fundamentals: build your first evaluation dataset,) Tj T*
(implement a CI/CD pipeline, and establish comprehensive monitoring. The Agent Starter) Tj T*
(Pack is a great place to start--it creates a production-ready agent project in minutes with) Tj T*
(these foundations already built-in.) Tj T*
(* If you're scaling, elevate your practice: automate the feedback loop from production) Tj T*
(insight to deployed improvement and standardize on interoperable protocols to build a) Tj T*
(cohesive ecosystem, not just point solutions.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
